cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "opentrash: open-source geospatial analytics for residential waste collection"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohamad
    family-names: Alsheikh Yassin
    affiliation: "AI Research Corps (AIRC)"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-07"
url: "https://opentrash.app/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/malsheikhyass/opentrash"
abstract: >
  opentrash is an open-source, cloud-native Python package for analyzing
  residential waste-collection operations. It ingests GPS telematics,
  parcel polygons, route polygons, and facility locations, performs one
  disciplined spatial-join pass, and produces two products: per-parcel
  service-signature detection (patterns) and interactive single-day route
  maps (RouteView). The design principle is "spatial joins are
  infrastructure; products are calculations."
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - waste-management
  - telematics
  - duckdb
  - geopandas
  - civic-technology
